<!--
	menus.xml - REQUIRED v3 file. Until this exists, the addon treats the skin as
	un-migrated and both type=manage and type=buildxml abort.

	SOURCES:
	  - Main menu items ............ mainmenu_DATA.xml
	  - Submenu items .............. {name}_DATA.xml (movies, tvshows, music, ...)
	  - shortcuts (search) menu .... shortcuts_DATA.xml
	  - overrides / icons / search / globaloverride / visibleoverride ... overrides.xml

	MAPPING NOTES:
	  - v2 <shortcut><defaultID>X</defaultID> ....... -> v3 <item name="X">
	  - v2 <label> / <action> / <visible> ........... -> kept verbatim
	  - empty <label2/> <icon/> <thumb/> placeholders -> omitted (no data)
	  - v2 mainmenu item "X" had submenu file X_DATA.xml -> <item submenu="X"> + <submenu name="X">
	  - v2 <visibleoverride group=.. condition=C>ACT</visibleoverride>
	        the comment in overrides.xml ("...when library has no content") indicates C gates the
	        NORMAL action and ACT is the empty-library fallback, so this becomes the documented v3
	        complementary-conditional-action pattern:
	            <action condition="C">{normal action}</action>
	            <action condition="!C">{ACT}</action>
	        Original v2 lines preserved as comments beside each affected item.

	FLAGS / WATCH-POINTS:
	  1. container="9000" on mainmenu is the v3 documented convention - VERIFY it matches the
	     main-menu list control id in your Home.xml. The shortcuts menu container is unknown
	     (no Home.xml provided) so it is omitted; add container="NNNN" if that menu uses one.
	  2. SUBMENU-level visibleoverrides (groups movies/tvshows/music/musicvideos) are preserved
	     as comments inside each submenu, NOT yet wired per-item, pending your confirmation of
	     intended per-item behavior (see summary).
	  3. <dialogs> (20 widget-slot subdialogs) - DONE. Buttons 501-520 each spawn a child dialog
	     with the correct property_suffix (.1-.20) and setfocus on the widget picker button.
	  4. Per-item background defaults (v2 backgrounddefault labelID=...) DEFERRED to after
	     backgrounds.xml exists, since v3 item background="..." references a background NAME.
	  5. <doNotShareMenu/> (v2) has no documented v3 equivalent; v3 stores per-skin userdata.json
	     natively, so menu sharing is not a concern. Recorded here, no action needed.
	  6. <groupings> below is NEWLY AUTHORED: your v2 overrides.xml had no shortcut-picker
	     groupings (it relied on skinshortcuts v2 built-in defaults, which v3 does not provide).
	     This is a functional starter derived from shortcuts_DATA.xml destinations - tune freely.
-->
